%description:

TcpCubic.beta:rfc9438 -- at a loss, the window goes down to 0.7 of its size.

The claim (TcpCubic.ned): "multiplicative-decrease factor applied to cwnd on loss (RFC 9438
section 4.6)".

The classes: rfc9438 (0.7, the default, the value of RFC 9438), other (another value between 0
and 1), invalid (0 and less, 1 and more). The code: TcpCubic::calculateSsthresh() returns
max(floor(segCwnd * beta), 2) segments; TcpCubic::initializeAlgorithm() checks the value. This test separates "rfc9438" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, with TcpCubic and without SACK, which sends 100000 bytes; the round
trip is 40 ms, and the tap drops the 15th data segment once. Observation: level 2, the first
slow-start threshold is 0.7 of the largest window before the loss.

%# parameter: TcpCubic.beta
%# class: rfc9438
%# value: 0.7
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.beta
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpCubicBetaRfc9438")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                                        .captureMax("cwndBefore", "value")
                                        .within(4.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                  .filterValueAtMost(1e8)
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      double ratio = context.event.value / context.get("cwndBefore").doubleValue();
                      return ratio >= 0.62 && ratio <= 0.78;
                  })
                  .describe("the threshold at the loss, 0.7 of the window")
                  .within(1.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpCubicBetaRfc9438 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.beta = 0.7    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpCubic"
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpCubicBetaRfc9438: PASS
